# Why One HashMap is Not Enough

Suppose

```text
s = "ab"

t = "cc"
```

If we only store

```text
a → c

b → c
```

Nothing appears wrong.

But

```text
c
```

is already used.

Therefore,

the mapping is invalid.

---

# Correct Approach

We need two maps.

```
Forward

a → c
```

and

```
Backward

c → a
```

Both mappings must remain consistent.

---

Visualization

```text
Forward

a → c

b → d
```

---

```text
Backward

c → a

d → b
```

If either mapping conflicts,

return

```text
false
```

---

# Algorithm

For every character

```text
Check forward mapping

↓

Check backward mapping

↓

Conflict?

↓

Return false

↓

Store mapping

↓

Continue
```

