# Alternative Approach

Since characters are ASCII,

we can replace HashMaps with arrays.

```java
class Solution {

    public boolean isIsomorphic(String s, String t) {

        int[] mapS = new int[256];
        int[] mapT = new int[256];

        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {

            char a = s.charAt(i);
            char b = t.charAt(i);

            if (mapS[a] != mapT[b]) {
                return false;
            }

            mapS[a] = i + 1;
            mapT[b] = i + 1;
        }

        return true;
    }
}
```

### Why `i + 1`?

Arrays are initialized with `0`.

Using `i + 1` distinguishes "not seen" (`0`) from the first position (`1`).

This is a common interview optimization.

