# Key Takeaways

- Frequency counting solves **"how many?"**
- Mapping solves **"who maps to whom?"**
- One HashMap is insufficient for enforcing one-to-one mappings.
- Two HashMaps (or two arrays for fixed alphabets) guarantee correctness.
- This pattern is foundational for many medium-level string and dictionary problems.

